<h2>Indian table grapes for export</h2>
<p>India's grape export business is built on timing. The season runs roughly January to April, filling the window between the end of Southern Hemisphere supply and the start of Northern Hemisphere harvests — which is why Nashik fruit ends up in European retail programmes despite an 18–28 day sea transit.</p>

<p>We supply Thompson Seedless, Flame Seedless, Sonaka and (seasonally) Crimson Seedless, pre-cooled promptly after harvest, packed with SO₂ generator pads, and shipped at 0–2°C.</p>

<h2>What makes or breaks a grape shipment?</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Pre-cooling speed.</strong> Grapes need field heat removed fast. Fruit that sits warm before pre-cooling loses shelf life you can never get back, no matter how well the container is set.</li>
  <li><strong>SO₂ pad management.</strong> Sulphur dioxide pads suppress botrytis over a long transit. Too little and you get mould; too much and you get bleaching. Packing specification should match the transit length to your port.</li>
  <li><strong>Residue compliance.</strong> For EU and UK buyers, pesticide residue testing isn't optional in practice. Agree it before shipment.</li>
  <li><strong>Berry size consistency.</strong> 16–18mm and 18mm+ are the common export grades. Mixed sizing within a carton is a frequent complaint on cheaper offers — specify your grade and we'll quote against it.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Which markets buy Indian grapes?</h2>
<p>The Netherlands is the principal European entry point (from where fruit redistributes across the EU), with Russia and the UK also taking significant volume, alongside the UAE and Bangladesh in regional markets. The data below shows what the available source reports — note that this particular dataset gives a ranked destination list without per-country values, so we've published the ranking rather than inventing figures to fill the gaps.</p>

<h2>Grape export pricing</h2>
<p>Grape pricing moves sharply within the short season — early-season fruit, peak-season volume and late-season tail all price differently, and reefer freight to Europe is a large share of landed cost. Send your variety, berry size, quantity and destination port for a current FOB or CIF quote.</p>

